
Lab 11: Configuring Smart Card Authentication
Objectives
By the end of this lab, students will be able to:

• Install and configure smart card middleware on a Linux system • Configure smart card authentication in Red Hat Identity Management (IdM) • Test smart card authentication for user login • Understand the security benefits of multi-factor authentication using smart cards • Troubleshoot common smart card authentication issues

Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, students should have:

• Basic understanding of Linux command line operations • Familiarity with Red Hat Identity Management (IdM) concepts • Knowledge of PKI (Public Key Infrastructure) fundamentals • Understanding of authentication and authorization concepts • Access to a Red Hat Enterprise Linux system with IdM installed

